    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0471" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg357"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00296A/86: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Basel</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cochran</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Basel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-23T18:00:00+01:00">December 23, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 23—12:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>For Castle. Final agreement on report reached this afternoon. Signing will take
                    place at 8:30 tonight. Press summary will be given out but the text will not be
                    issued for several hours. Since these will both be telegraphed by the Associated
                    Press, I shall not cable but mail text.<anchor n="51a" xml:id="d267-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cochran</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d267-f1" n="51a" xml:id="d267-f1-content">
                <p>For text, see Great Britain, Cmd. 3995, Germany No. 1 (1932): <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Report of the Special Advisory Committee convened under
                        the Agreement with Germany concluded at The Hague on January 20, 1930</hi>,
                    Basle, December 23, 1931.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
